  "vegSub": "MVS 36 · Temperate tussock grassland · in Victoria's terms, Plains Grassland (EVC 132), Victorian Volcanic Plain",
  "intro": "Before 1750 your address on Kurweeton Road, in the shadow of Mount Elephant, stood in open, almost treeless grassland on the basalt plains of the Western District: a sea of Kangaroo Grass, tussock and wallaby grasses, threaded with lilies, daisies and Murnong that flowered in waves through spring. Trees grew only along drainage lines and on the stony rises. These grasslands are among the most cleared ecosystems in Australia and are listed nationally as Critically Endangered (Natural Temperate Grassland of the Victorian Volcanic Plain), so even a small patch brought back genuinely matters. The plants below are indigenous to this grassland and grouped by the layer they fill. Here the grasses are the framework; plant them first and let the wildflowers live between the tussocks.",
